#+TITLE: Require native COM quiescence before opening the job DWG
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-com-job-drawing

* Evidence
SCHME !339 BricsCAD jobs 564960, 564958 and 565290 lose their application
before READY, at app.HWND, after Documents.Open/Activate. Windows events for
564960 record BricsCAD faults in KERNELBASE.dll and ntdll.dll. The bridge opens
the requested DWG immediately after CreateObject responds, and only then
captures the owned process. The exact native crash cause remains unconfirmed.

* Correction under qualification
Both COM emitters require GetAcadState().IsQuiescent before Documents.Open,
with a bounded 30-second check. Capture the exact created application's window
process identity before opening the file, so a file-open crash does not erase
the ownership evidence. No attach/replacement instance lookup and no fallback
to a blank drawing. A failed readiness check remains a startup failure.

* References
- https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2024/KOR/AutoCAD-ActiveX-Reference/files/GUID-820F93B4-7B83-4708-8E21-0D43D7D1C828.htm
- https://developer.bricsys.com/bricscad/help/en_US/V9/DevRef/source/IDR_VBA_Objects953.htm
